WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:07.569
Long lines at fuel stations, drivers waiting
patiently.. but without much hope.

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:12.910
Most gas stations in Mexico have run out of
fuel since the government shut down a major

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:17.110
pipeline and started delivering gas by tanker
trucks only.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:26.020
The truth is, it's really bad, because we
already went to several gas stations and we

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.349
didn't find gasoline.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:35.200
It´s been three days already
It's a disaster, it's a disaster everywhere,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.900
I've been to two gas stations and they don't
have any.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.980
Look at this, where else do you have to go?

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.810
If there isn't any here, where else do you
have to go?

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:50.300
For years, criminals have tapped into pipelines,
stealing millions of litres of fuel and depriving

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:56.000
the state-run oil monopoly PEMEX of over 7
billion dollars in revenue.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.010
That's according to government estimates.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.570
This is not 'petty theft'.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:12.330
We're talking about major robbery, one-thousand
attacks on the pipeline per day, 15,000 liters

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:18.729
stolen each time!

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:21.950
How do they distribute all that stolen gasoline?

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:36.950
Well, there was an attitude of total complicity
on the part of PEMEX

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:42.710
Violent criminal gangs have long relied on
fuel theft to supplement their income.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:48.710
But, says the government, accomplices within
the industry also seem to be a major part

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:49.420
of the problem.

